# Lume GitHub analyzer — environment
#
# Copy to .env and adjust (or export these before `make dev`).
# .env is gitignored — keep your real OWNER / GH_TOKEN out of the repo so the
# project can be shared publicly.
# .env is loaded by the shell (scripts/env.sh + dev.sh), never by `make
# -include .env`: make would turn every key into a make variable and print
# GH_TOKEN / LLM_API_KEY in `make -pn` / debug output. Already-set env vars
# win over .env, so `OWNER=foo make fetch` still fetches foo.

# Your GitHub login. Used as:
#   - the default owner until data/github/last_owner exists (a `make fetch`
#     run writes it)
#   - the ONLY owner whose follower/following lists get the water-account /
#     recruiter pre-screen (suspects.json) merged into /api/people
# Leave empty to use data/github/last_owner once present.
OWNER=

# Optional: raise the unauthenticated 60 req/h -> 5000 req/h limit on the
# GitHub API. Used by the server's live proxy (/api/live/github), the people
# refresh (/api/refresh), scripts/fetch-github.sh, people-scan.sh and
# unfollow.sh. NEVER commit a real token.
# Least privilege: reads (snapshots / trending / live) work with a classic
# token that has NO scopes (still 5000 req/h), or a fine-grained token limited
# to public repositories (read-only). Only follow/unfollow needs `user:follow`
# — prefer a separate token for that (or leave those actions unused).
# GH_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional: route GitHub outbound HTTP through a local proxy (Clash / V2Ray
# etc). lume's http_get/http_put read LUME_HTTP_PROXY as an override; without
# it the dev server goes direct. A proxy is steadier against the mainland's
# intermittent TLS resets to api.github.com.
# LUME_HTTP_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:7897

# Optional: shift the server port if 8091 is taken.
# LUME_GITHUB_PORT=9000

# --- Agent (LLM chat) ---
# The /chat agent and the repo_insights / people tools use Lume's built-in LLM
# bridge (OpenAI-compatible endpoint). Leave all three unset to get the
# canned offline engine instead (works, but no real model answers).
#   LLM_API_URL  — endpoint, e.g. https://api.openai.com/v1 (or a local
#                  vLLM/Ollama-compatible server)
#   LLM_API_KEY  — secret; NEVER commit a real key
#   LLM_MODEL    — model id, e.g. gpt-4o-mini
#   LLM_TIMEOUT  — seconds to wait on the upstream LLM stream (default 60)
# LLM_API_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# LLM_TIMEOUT=60
#
# The trending tab reuses this endpoint to translate repository descriptions
# into Chinese when the UI is Chinese. The server reads the key under the
# alias LLM_ANALYZER_KEY because .lume's env() masks *API_KEY* names; dev.sh
# and docker-compose.yml derive it from LLM_API_KEY automatically, so normally
# you set nothing extra. Override only if you want a separate key for
# translation. Leave unset/empty to disable translation (English is shown).
# LLM_ANALYZER_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# Translation tuning (all optional):
#   TR_TRANSLATE_BATCH   — descriptions per gateway call (default 6). A single
#                          call carrying every missing description is slow and
#                          some upstreams reject a large JSON array; keep this
#                          small so each call finishes inside the timeout on a
#                          free/flash model.
#   TR_TRANSLATE_TIMEOUT — per-attempt seconds (default 20); free upstreams can
#                          cold-start near ~30s.
#   TR_TRANSLATE_RETRIES — attempts per chunk before giving up (default 3).
# A single chunk that fails every retry no longer aborts the rest — only two
# consecutive dead chunks are treated as a down gateway. When the whole batch
# translates nothing, the response is NOT cached (a transient outage must not
# serve English as `tr=zh` for the cache TTL). See app/lib/trending.lume.
# TR_TRANSLATE_BATCH=6
# TR_TRANSLATE_TIMEOUT=20
# TR_TRANSLATE_RETRIES=3

# Optional: raw text APPENDED to the agent's system prompt (single line; the
# .env loader reads line by line, so no line breaks inside the value).
# Use it for scenario guidance the agent should always follow — e.g. which
# data to answer from, how to cite evidence, output language:
# LLM_SYSTEM_EXTRA="You are a GitHub talent-signal analyst. Base answers on
# the local snapshot (data/github/<owner>/snapshot.json) and /api/* results,
# cite concrete repo names and numbers as evidence, never invent data."

# Optional: extra origins appended to the server's Content-Security-Policy
# img-src (space-separated). The server reads AGENTHTTPD_CSP_IMG_SRC at
# response time; default policy is img-src 'self' data:.
# Used here to allow GitHub avatar CDNs:
# AGENTHTTPD_CSP_IMG_SRC=https://avatars.githubusercontent.com

# Optional: TTL in seconds for the /api/live/github response cache (default
# 300, 0 disables). Repeated views of the same profile are served from the
# in-memory cache to save GitHub rate limit and latency.
# LIVE_CACHE_TTL_SEC=300
# Optional: TTL in seconds for the disk tier of the /api/live/github cache
# (default 86400 = 24h, 0 disables). Successful live responses are persisted
# under data/github/live/ so agent tools and every browser reuse them across
# server restarts; stale entries are pruned on make dev (older than 3 days).
# LIVE_DISK_TTL_SEC=86400

# Optional: TTL in seconds for the /api/trending response cache — memory
# TRENDING_CACHE_TTL_SEC (default 120) and disk TRENDING_DISK_TTL_SEC
# (default 600); 0 disables either. github.com/trending reorders every few
# minutes, so the defaults are deliberately short; `?refresh=1` (the UI refresh
# button and make trending-push) bypasses both tiers to fetch fresh.
# TRENDING_CACHE_TTL_SEC=120
# TRENDING_DISK_TTL_SEC=600

# Optional: server bind address (default 127.0.0.1 = loopback-only). Docker
# sets LUME_GITHUB_BIND=0.0.0.0 in docker-compose.yml so the mapped host port
# can reach the container — the host port itself stays 127.0.0.1, so nothing
# is exposed to the network either way. Native installs should leave this
# unset.
# LUME_GITHUB_BIND=0.0.0.0

# --- Water-account pre-screen (people-suspects.py) ---
# The heuristic thresholds are no longer hard-coded. Pick a judgment call with
# SUSPECT_MODE, or override individual knobs on top. All defaults reproduce
# the historic behavior (verified by scripts/suspects-selftest.py).
#   standard — recent = est. 2024+, high = 2025+ WITH a login pattern
#   strict   — flags MORE: recent = 2022+, high = 2023+ (a new year alone counts)
#   lenient  — flags FEWER (higher confidence): recent = 2025+ AND pattern,
#              high = 2026+ with >= 2 patterns
# Individual overrides (set any to override the mode's value):
#   SUSPECT_RECENT_BOUND=the math      oldest est. year counted "recent" (medium base)
#   SUSPECT_HIGH_BOUND=the math        oldest est. year that can be "high"
#   SUSPECT_HIGH_NEEDS_PATTERN=0|1     high tier also requires a login pattern
#   SUSPECT_PATTERN_MIN=2              patterns required for a high flag
#   SUSPECT_RECENT_NEEDS_PATTERN=0|1   medium tier also requires a pattern
#   SUSPECT_USE_UID=0                  ignore the avatar-uid age signal: age becomes
#                                      unknown and only login patterns flag (medium)
#   SUSPECT_BUZZWORDS=zorb,quux        comma list REPLACING the buzz-word set
#   SUSPECT_BATCH_NAMES=zhongqiu       comma list REPLACING the batch-name set
# SUSPECT_MODE=standard

# --- Group webhook push (钉钉自定义机器人 / 企微 / Server酱) ---
# Optional: push the GitHub trending board (make trending-push) and, with
# NOTIFY=1, the daily summary (make daily) to a group chat. Both are OPT-IN —
# nothing is sent unless a URL is configured and you actually run the push.
#   TREND_WEBHOOK_URL     the robot's webhook URL (empty = push disabled)
#   TREND_WEBHOOK_SECRET  DingTalk 「加签」 secret; leave empty when the robot
#                         uses a keyword (e.g. "GitHub") or an IP allowlist
#   TREND_WEBHOOK_KEYWORD the keyword for a keyword-secured robot; prepended to
#                         every message body so ANY push (trending + daily)
#                         passes keyword inspection. 加签 / IP mode leaves it empty.
# DingTalk URL form:  https://oapi.dingtalk.com/robot/send?access_token=XXX
#   make trending-push                 # push today's trending (top 10, Chinese)
#   NOTIFY=1 make daily                # also push the daily change summary
#   NOTIFY_YES=1 make daily            # skip the "contains others' logins" warning
#   REDACT_LOGINS=1 make daily         # push masked logins (`er***en`) instead
#   DRY_RUN=1 make trending-push       # preview the message without sending
# TREND_WEBHOOK_URL=
# TREND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# TREND_WEBHOOK_KEYWORD=

# Optional: how long to keep local PII (agent chat transcripts under
# .data/sessions). `make purge` removes files older than this; 0 disables.
# Snapshot dirs are only removed explicitly via `make purge-owner OWNER=<login>`.
# SESSIONS_TTL_DAYS=30

# Optional: base URL of the running lume server that make trending-push reads
# /api/trending from (translated + cached). Default is
# http://127.0.0.1:${LUME_GITHUB_PORT:-8091}; use http://127.0.0.1:18091 for
# the Docker container, or a URL to push from a different machine. When the
# server is unreachable the push falls back to the GitHub Search API directly.
# TREND_PUSH_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8091

# Optional: push defaults (overridable per run via make SINCE=/TOP=/LANG_FILTER=).
# TREND_PUSH_SINCE=daily     # daily | weekly | monthly | quarterly | year
# TREND_PUSH_TOP=10          # how many repos the message lists
# TREND_PUSH_LANG=           # language filter, e.g. Python / Go (empty = all)
